lesson k-tap-shake-and-blow v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=1 subject=music levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Tap, shake and blow"
  goal "Say how an instrument is played: tapped, shaken, blown or plucked."

  look {
    scene 26x8 {
      drum d lugs=5 at=canvas(1, 1)
      chimebars c bars=6 letters=0 right-of=d gap=2
    }
    say """
        Instruments make sounds in different ways. You tap a drum and chime bars, shake a shaker, blow
        a recorder and pluck a guitar's strings. Each way makes its own kind of sound.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.how-to-play k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.how-to-play count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2
    show k.drum-tap
    practice k.count-bars count=2 seed=3
    show k.strings-or-skin k=0 hard-k=1
    show k.make-a-shaker
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.why-drum-sounds
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.tapped-count k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "Tap it, shake it, blow it or pluck it: each instrument has its way."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. This is the first music lesson of the year, before the steady beat:
    the instruments the later lessons play. Pots, a wooden spoon and a bottle of rice are a whole
    band. The shaker is for you to watch. If the child is stuck, act out playing each instrument.
    Off the page, listen to a piece of music and guess which instruments you hear. Japan,
    幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 表現, 内容 (6):
    "音楽に親しみ，歌を歌ったり，簡単なリズム楽器を使ったりなどする楽しさを味わう。" (Enjoy music, singing songs
    and playing simple rhythm instruments.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the drum is worked in the teacher's pen first, the instruments are a drum, a shaker and a recorder, and the chime bars are few."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the instruments are a guitar, a triangle and a trumpet, there are more bars, and the three-star counts what you blow."
  }
}
